# Concept A (scaled quad tailsitter, J6 board D-182) - ArduPilot Plane parameter file, DRAFT QP-2-R1 (owner F4 / B3, 2026-11-14; D-183 props/pack, D-184 arm x1.2 + cant 16 deg; D-189 cant 17, D-191 pitch and yaw rate gains)
# QP-4 FIXES 2026-11-15: Q_WVANE_ENABLE 0 (turbulence test failed); elevon span y 0.04-0.35 (SERVO5/6 MIN/MAX still to be bench-set for +-20 deg); balance D-187 v2 in cad/a_model.py. SITL (FIXES.md) re-run on roll rate, transition at 1.43 / 1.50 kg, back-transition (pilot yaw, vane off).
# QP-4 fold-in 2026-11-15 (BOARD QP-3 s1 item 10, s3 D-186): harmonic notch re-based on hover 1P 100-119 Hz and set to the throttle reference until M4 confirms bidirectional DShot; BDMASK 0 until then; FC hard-mounted; leg 150 m; Q_WVANE conditional. SITL was NOT re-run on this edit (the SITL runner skips INS_HNTCH / SERVO_BLH lines).
# Status: PROPOSED, starting set only. Not loaded on hardware. SITL ran a hover-only JSON model of A (qp/A/sitl/SITL-A.md);
#   gains and hover limits below are tuned on that EST model, so every one is a bench-test starting value, not a result.
# Derived from subsystems/flight-software/K09L.param R11 (names checked there against ArduPlane 4.7.x, SITL 4.7.3-beta1).
#   A-specific changes are marked "A:". Lines kept from K09-L carry the K09-L lesson in the comment.
# Source of A's numbers: redesign/qp/sizing_A/sizing_a.py (mass 1.23-1.37 kg, MN2212 KV780, 9545, 4S), review/QP-1/BOARD.md C1-C8.
# Board-only lines (not in SITL): SERVO_BLH_BDMASK, SERVO_BLH_POLES. Board choice (Kakute or CoreWing, BOARD C6) is open:
#   BATT_VOLT_MULT / BATT_AMP_PERVLT, SERIALn, GPS/INS offsets and RC maps below are the K09-L CoreWing values or "-" (omitted).
# Frame: x aft, y right, z up in cruise. Hover copter frame: forward = belly, right = right wing, down = tail. Motor map as K09-L.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1 Frame: copter-motor tailsitter (K09-L unchanged)
# enable the QuadPlane VTOL code (reboot after setting)
Q_ENABLE,1
# tailsitter on the quad motors
Q_TAILSIT_ENABLE,1
# frame class 1 = Quad (K09-L lesson: class 1, not 10, so the tailsitter defaults table is NOT applied; Q_A_ANGLE_BOOST is set below)
Q_FRAME_CLASS,1
# X frame: A=output 1, B=4, C=2, D=3 (K09-L S2 test), same wiring as K09-L
Q_FRAME_TYPE,1
# all four motors run in fixed-wing flight (no pusher)
Q_TAILSIT_MOTMX,15
# Q_OPTIONS 262400 = bit 8 (assist keeps plane pitch controller) + bit 18, as K09-L (R8 lesson: see K09L.param)
Q_OPTIONS,262400
# boot in QSTABILIZE (K09-L R-SPIRAL: a reset in the air must come up in a manual hover mode)
INITIAL_MODE,17
SERVO1_FUNCTION,33
SERVO2_FUNCTION,34
SERVO3_FUNCTION,35
SERVO4_FUNCTION,36
# elevons (K09-L map). QP-4: the drawn elevon is y 0.04-0.34 m with +-20 deg stops (BOARD s1 item 3); SERVO5/6 MIN/MAX below are K09-L pulse values: set them so full travel = +-20 deg when the servo is calibrated (bench), and re-run SITL with the 20 deg stop
# BUILD NOTE (SERVO.md, D6): elevon servo is the EMAX ES3054HV (6.0-8.4 V, 20.5 g). The Kakute servo BEC defaults to 5.3 V = below the servo's rating: SET THE FC SERVO RAIL JUMPER TO 7.2 V before the first power-up with servos fitted (Kakute F405 Wing Mini: 5.3 V default / 7.2 V selectable, 3 A).
SERVO5_FUNCTION,77
SERVO6_FUNCTION,78
# DShot600 on outputs 1-4 (needs the DShot ESC of BOARD C6)
Q_M_PWM_TYPE,5
# QP-4 (BOARD s3): 0 until the Kakute reads rpm from the SpeedyBee on the bench (M4). ArduPilot's DShot ESC page says bidirectional DShot is for BLHeli32 / AM32 ESCs, and stock BLHeli_S J-H-40 (this ESC's page) is not listed (FOLDIN s3); the wrong firmware can give unpredictable motor behaviour. Set 15 only after M4 passes (and with Bluejay if that is what M4 needs)
SERVO_BLH_BDMASK,0
# MN2212 = 12N14P = 14 poles (K09-L value 14 was for its own motor; A: 14 from the 12N14P winding, check the datasheet - not read)
# 14 poles: MN2212 is 12N14P (page not read). Only used with bidirectional DShot rpm
SERVO_BLH_POLES,14
SERVO_DSHOT_ESC,1
SERVO5_REVERSED,1
SERVO5_TRIM,1500
SERVO5_MIN,1003
SERVO5_MAX,1976
SERVO6_REVERSED,0
SERVO6_TRIM,1500
SERVO6_MIN,1024
SERVO6_MAX,1997
MIXING_GAIN,0.65

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 2 Motors and thrust
# A: spin cap 0.90, REQUIRED (D-183): APC 9x4.5MR uncapped full duty is 13.0 A (14.3 A one motor at 1.50 kg) vs the 13 A / 180 s rating; at 0.90 one motor is 12.1 A phase / 10.9 A bus (prop_a.py).
#   SITL: with this cap the hover cases in wind never need more than the numbers in SITL-A.md; K09-L lesson: the motor has no burst rating
# T-083: Q_M_SPIN_MAX 1.0: the X2216 needs no motor-current cap (one motor 20.1 A fresh vs the 24.9 A EST line); a 0.90 cap would cut the sag window to +4.6 % (no download, prop_a --sched at 1.912 kg). Was 0.90 (MN2212, A-P16).
Q_M_SPIN_MAX,1.0
# A: pack limit. sizing_a.py peak pack current 41 A (4 x 10.3 A table at 100 %); no limiter needed below that - EST
Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX,72
Q_M_BAT_IDX,0
Q_M_BAT_CURR_TC,1
# 4S LiPo full / empty (3.3 V/cell). Thrust compensation by voltage is ON (K09-L R10 practice); SITL has no battery model so it is inert there
Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MAX,16.8
Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN,13.2
# spin-min 0.15 (K09-L); A hover thrust 396 gf/motor at the 1.47 kg gate (cant 17, was 402 at 1.50 kg and cant 16) = 0.35 of the 1138 gf APC table maximum (prop_a.py, x0.93 derate)
Q_M_SPIN_MIN,0.15
# A: expo 0.55, a fit of the maker's table (u 0.5 / 0.65 / 0.75 / 0.85 -> 0.32 / 0.52 / 0.66 / 0.81 of full thrust gives expo 0.72 / 0.58 / 0.49 / 0.33); K09-L 0.65. EST
Q_M_THST_EXPO,0.55
# A: hover in thrust space is 0.36 fresh (0.46 on the sagged pack); start in between, learned in flight
Q_M_THST_HOVER,0.42
Q_M_HOVER_LEARN,2
# fixed-wing throttle limit. QP-3 follow-up 1 (SITL-FLIGHT.md Follow-ups): the FC passes THR_MAX straight to the motor duty (SITL read-back: 80 -> 0.800, 60 -> 0.600), so 80 gave a
#   FRESH-pack level speed of 22.0 m/s (a_aero / fu_level.py, confirmed 21.9 m/s in SITL) = the structures VD 22, 1.2 x VC above the 17.6 m/s that VD 22 allows (VH <= VD / 1.25) and above AIRSPEED_MAX 18.
#   QP-4: D-186 ruling THR_MAX 68 + FWD_BAT 16.8 / 13.2 accepted; condition: the first cruise logs duty at 17 m/s (M8); above 0.65 fresh -> THR_MAX 70 + VD 25 only once the elevon stop is 20 deg (hinge ratio about 1.85 EST), else a higher-pitch prop (C7). VD is 24 (flutter / divergence estimate required before the wing is cut, G8).
#   Fix = the FWD_BAT compensation K09-L used (lines below, 16.8 / 13.2 V, already in the file): the ceiling becomes THR_MAX x 16.8 V / resting voltage, so the motor terminal voltage at the ceiling
#   is the same on every pack. 68: ceiling duty 0.68 fresh, 0.77 at 14.92 V rest, 0.87 at 13.2 V rest; level speed 18.7-18.8 m/s fresh (the maximum over pack states), 18.6-18.7 sagged, 18.5 empty;
#   17 m/s needs duty 0.62 fresh / 0.70 sagged, so the margin to the ceiling is 0.06-0.07 on every pack state and the climb at 17 m/s is 2.2-3.2 m/s (EST). SITL with compensation on (THR_MAX 66, SIM_BATT_VOLTAGE 14.92 / 16.8):
#   ceiling duty 0.750 / 0.660 as predicted (0.743 / 0.660), CRUISE held 17.2 m/s at duty 0.705 sagged / 0.621 fresh. C1 VD 24 (VH 18.8 x 1.25 = 23.5): REQUIRED, see STRUCTURES / SITL-FLIGHT follow-up 1. EST until C7 / thrust stand
THR_MAX,68
FWD_BAT_VOLT_MAX,16.8
FWD_BAT_VOLT_MIN,13.2
FWD_BAT_IDX,0
THR_MIN,10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 3 Hover attitude (tuned on the SITL EST model, QP-2)
# A: lean limit 45 deg (D-184 keeps it; board C2 "Q_ANGLE_MAX about 45"). In ArduPlane 4.7.3-beta1 SITL there is NO Q_ANGLE_MAX (read back: absent); the limit is
#   Q_A_ANGLE_MAX in degrees (stock 30, K09-L left it at 30). Sizing: lean 29 deg at 5 m/s broadside, 47 deg at 7 m/s. SITL-A.md shows what the cases need
Q_A_ANGLE_MAX,45
# Q_LOIT_ANG_MAX (stock 15) and Q_P_NE_* are left at the stock values: raising Q_LOIT_ANG_MAX to 40 changed nothing in SITL, and Q_P_NE_VEL_I 1.5 / Q_P_NE_POS_P 1.0
#   made the 5 m/s belly hover oscillate (lean 31-35 deg, yaw 11 deg). Position hold at 29 deg lean is an open tuning item (SITL-A.md)
# hover body-rate limits (deg/s), K09-L values
Q_A_RATE_R_MAX,120
Q_A_RATE_P_MAX,120
Q_A_RATE_Y_MAX,90
# A: roll/pitch rate loop. K09-L 0.08 was for 2.6 kg / 5.5 s of pack; A has I_z 0.05 and I_y 0.03 kg m2 (EST, a_plant.py) so P is higher. Starting values
# QP-3 follow-up 2 (SITL-FLIGHT.md Follow-ups; sitl/fu_cage.py): the cage flex modes (pitch 12-15 Hz, yaw 8-10 Hz, roll 29-35 Hz in the iteration-2 FE) are above the 2-4 Hz rate crossover.
#   With P 0.25 / D 0.004, gyro filter 40 Hz and D filter 32 Hz the pitch loop is unstable or has gain margin 1.0-1.7 over the three property corners and zeta 0.3-1 % (the
#   lag of the motor, gyro and D filters turns the 12-15 Hz mode into a pole). Lower P, D and LESS lag restore it (pitch 15 / 0.002 / FLTD 40 + gyro 60: min gain margin 2.8; roll 0.20 / 0.003 / 32 + gyro 60: 2.5).
#   D-191 (CLAIMS-FIX): with the tap-test tolerance +-20 % on the cage modes the 0.15 / 0.002 / 40 set had pitch GM 1.56-1.64 (< 2). Pitch P 0.12 / D 0.0012 / FLTD 60 (gyro 60 kept): GM 2.33 over every corner, damping, thrust scale and mode shift of 0.8-1.2 (sitl/fu_cage.py; structures/iter3_run.md); rigid crossover 2.2 Hz (was 2.6), PM 54 deg (was 56), Ms 2.2 (was 2.7).
#   QP-4 / D-186: the FC stays on the wing-centre plate as drawn, HARD-MOUNTED (thin foam tape), NOT on the 5 mm gel pads (their stiffness is unknown; a gel mode could sit in the rate band or on hover 1P). Gel only if its frequency is measured at 40-70 Hz.
#   REQUIRES the flight controller hard-mounted on the wing spar (C4: spar centre; D-239/D-240: 75 mm left of centre, y -75 mm, to cut the 27-30 Hz wing-flap pickup: model result, T-091; unconfirmed until T-A-TAP / tether), not on the cage hub: with the IMU on the hub the yaw (8-10 Hz) and roll (29-35 Hz) loops are unstable at zeta <= 1 % with any of these settings.
Q_A_RAT_RLL_P,0.20
Q_A_RAT_RLL_I,0.25
Q_A_RAT_RLL_D,0.003
Q_A_RAT_RLL_FLTD,32
Q_A_RAT_PIT_P,0.12
Q_A_RAT_PIT_I,0.25
Q_A_RAT_PIT_D,0.0012
Q_A_RAT_PIT_FLTD,60
# yaw: A's yaw authority comes from cant 17 deg (D-189) + arm x1.2 + reaction (model 0.363 N m at +-0.10 throttle EST; the hanging yaw test must confirm >= 0.35, fail < 0.30). P 0.37 (was 0.40, D-191): the longer yaw lever of cant 17 raised the loop gain 4.8 %; 0.37 restores the gain margin (fu_cage.py: 2.09 with the cage modes +-20 %)
Q_A_RAT_YAW_P,0.37
Q_A_RAT_YAW_I,0.04
# yaw acceleration limit deg/s/s (K09-L; A has a smaller I_x so this could rise)
Q_A_ACC_Y_MAX,135
# descent and landing: K09-L (A's sizing 1.2 m/s hard-landing load 12 g, so the final 0.3 m/s stays)
Q_WP_SPD_DN,1.2
Q_PILOT_SPD_DN,1.0
Q_LAND_FINAL_SPD,0.3
Q_LAND_FINAL_ALT,6
# Weathervane: QP-2 / D-184 had it OFF because mode 1 (nose = belly into wind) is the wrong way for A (lean 30 deg, hold 4.7 m off). Wind rule: pilot holds the wing edge into the wind within +-10 deg (+-20 deg steady only), belly-on only to 3 m/s; limit 5 m/s mean, gust <= 8 m/s
# QP-4 / D-186: ACCEPTED CONDITIONALLY. Proven in calm SITL only (lean feedback: turbulence may make it chase gusts). Before the first free hover: SITL with WIND.md's 1 m/s turbulence model, heading excursion <= 15 deg; card QLOITER -> QSTABILIZE -> FBWA within 2 s (M9 tether check). If it fails, set Q_WVANE_ENABLE 0 and fly the pilot-yaw rule.
# QP-3 follow-up 5 (heading cue): 3 = SIDE into wind = the wing edge, which is what A needs (the QP-2 OFF decision was for 1 = nose/belly into wind). Q_WVANE_GAIN defaults to 0 on Plane
#   (= no weathervane at all, why a bare ENABLE 3 does nothing), so it is set; SPD_MAX 2 keeps it off while the ground speed is above 2 m/s (back-transition). SITL, 1.50 kg, 5 m/s wind from the belly:
#   QLOITER hover turns to within 6-8 deg of edge-on in about 12 s and holds it (lean 8.4 deg against 25 deg belly-on); after a head-wind back-transition (peak duty 0.81, no cap) it turned 1 -> 86 deg in 26 s
#   and landed edge-on. It acts only in position-controlled Q modes with the yaw stick centred for 2 s; the pilot yaw stick overrides. FLIGHT CARD: before the pitch-over yaw the belly to the flight
#   heading and go QLOITER -> QSTABILIZE -> FBWA within 2 s, otherwise the aircraft turns edge-on first and the back-transition ends up crosswind (2.2-2.4 s at the 0.90 cap at 5 m/s, SITL)
# QP-4 FIXES 2026-11-15 (D6/B3): Q_WVANE_ENABLE BACK TO 0. The turbulence condition above FAILED (ASDRAWN.md s2.5: heading excursion 15.4-23.7 deg at gain 1, 11.4-19.4 at gain 0.5, limit 15, 5 of 7 runs over). Per D-184 the heading in a hover is the pilot's yaw stick (wing edge into the wind within +-10 deg) and the QLOITER -> QSTABILIZE -> FBWA card applies; no automatic weathervane. Gain and speed limit kept at their values so a later re-test only has to set ENABLE 3.
Q_WVANE_ENABLE,0
Q_WVANE_GAIN,1
Q_WVANE_SPD_MAX,2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 4 Transition (K09-L lessons, A numbers where they exist)
# pitch-over rate cap 12 deg/s (K09-L B3 entry law, A's sizing used the same 12 deg/s to 70 deg). QP-3 SITL ran the entry (held throttle, 1.0 s pre-climb in QSTABILIZE, then FBWA):
#   transmitter throttle override = static T/W 1.33-1.42 at the sag state (window centre 1.38 at 1.50 kg, 1.44 at 1.381 kg); at the learnt Q_M_THST_HOVER about 0.46-0.51 in SITL that is a
#   stick of about 1790-1800 us. The K09-L ratio 1.285 x learnt hover throttle gives T/W 1.285 = BELOW A's 1.33 low edge (still flew, but see SITL-FLIGHT.md). Pre-climb 0 raises elevon use from 0.53 to 0.91
Q_TAILSIT_RAT_FW,12
# inert while RAT_FW is set (K09-L); kept so the firmware would derive 70 / (11.667 / 2) = 12 deg/s
Q_TRANSITION_MS,11667
# K09-L R8: boost must be SET to 0 (class 1 does not get the tailsitter defaults); throttle held through the pitch-over
Q_A_ANGLE_BOOST,0
Q_THROTTLE_EXPO,0.2
# back-transition pitch-up rate and throttle (K09-L: slower pitch-up balloons more, stage A S5a); A: unverified, stage B needed
# QP-3 follow-up 3: 30 deg/s put the motors at the 0.90 cap for 0.56 s at the 1.50 kg gate (no wind, 17 m/s entry). 24: no cap in 0 and 5 m/s head wind (peak duty 0.88 / 0.81, balloon 6.2 / 5.4 m,
#   pitch-up 8 s, 102 m of travel to 3 m/s against 82). 18: peak 0.83, 126 m of travel. Do NOT lower Q_TAILSIT_THR_VT (40: 3-5 s at the cap, lean 64 deg). Entry speed 15 instead of 17 changed nothing (0.26 s at cap)
Q_TAILSIT_RAT_VT,24
Q_TAILSIT_ANGLE,70
Q_TAILSIT_ANG_VT,0
Q_TAILSIT_THR_VT,55
Q_TAILSIT_GSCMSK,1
# A: disk loading 66 N/m2 = 6.7 kg/m2 (sizing_a.py; K09-L 10.6)
Q_TAILSIT_DSKLD,6.7
# Q-assist: OFF in angle and altitude (K09-L: assist adds no lift on the same motors and bypasses the 35 deg/s clamp); speed assist below 13 m/s
Q_ASSIST_SPEED,13
Q_ASSIST_ALT,0
Q_ASSIST_ANGLE,0
# failed transition: QRTL after 15 s (K09-L)
Q_TRANS_FAIL,15
Q_TRANS_FAIL_ACT,1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 5 Fixed wing (A: cruise 17 m/s, Vs 11.76 / 12.19 m/s at 1.396 / 1.50 kg EST, MISSION.md s1; QP-3 SITL-FLIGHT.md)
# T-101 D-255 (AM-059): cruise 18 m/s (cuts the elevon cruise trim about 1 deg; with the pack at the aft end of its tray slot, CG 23.49 mm, pitch use 0.59 worst of the four C3 cases).
#   Margin to the THR_MAX 68 ceiling shrinks: level speed at the ceiling 18.5-18.8 m/s (above); SITL A1 settled at 18.1-18.3 m/s (0.2-0.7 m/s headroom). Checked on the first cruise logs (duty, M8 / TP-11).
AIRSPEED_CRUISE,18
# integer parameter (14.5 read back as 14 in SITL). 1.3 x Vs = 14.3, so 15; K09-L kept MIN = cruise
AIRSPEED_MIN,16
# D-255: 20 (was 18 = the new cruise); below the maximum level speed is not required, VD 24 m/s (A-P13) bounds it
AIRSPEED_MAX,20
AIRSPEED_STALL,12.2
# QP-3: servo-gain scaling speed = cruise (was 15, left from the 15 m/s draft). Not tested separately in SITL (FBWA / CRUISE flew stable at 17 m/s with the stock gains, elevon peak 8.6 deg)
SCALING_SPEED,17
ROLL_LIMIT_DEG,45
PTCH_LIM_MAX_DEG,20
PTCH_LIM_MIN_DEG,-10
# D-254 / D-255: roll-rate demand cap = the derived cruise roll requirement (MIL-F-8785C Class I L1 Cat B, 60 deg in 1.7 s, about 45 deg/s); was 150.
#   TCONST 0.9 (ArduPlane default 0.5) trims the bank overshoot a little (SITL, one sample each: elevon 18.14 -> 17.36 deg; 60 deg change from the bank at the reversal command in 1.50 s,
#   1.81 s from the commanded +30 to -30 deg). Flight tune at TP-11.
RLL2SRV_RMAX,45
RLL2SRV_TCONST,0.9
# pitch-rate caps (K09-L: from its torsion mode and CL-F4-PTCH-RMAX-TURN). A: a 45 deg bank level turn at 15 m/s needs g tan(phi) sin(phi) / V = 26.5 deg/s
#   (K09-L 17 m/s: 23.4), so UP 35 still covers it. No A structural basis for the cap yet (fin f1 / wing torsion not computed): keep the K09-L numbers
PTCH2SRV_RMAX_UP,35
PTCH2SRV_RMAX_DN,20
# QP-3 follow-up 1: climb attainable at 17 m/s at the THR_MAX 68 ceiling is 2.8-3.2 m/s fresh, 2.2-2.5 m/s at 13.2 V rest (EST); the cap follows the worst state
TECS_CLMB_MAX,2
TECS_SINK_MAX,2.5
# T-101 / D-251 C3 control: pitch weights height over speed so TECS does not chop throttle after CRUISE handover; SITL pitch use at the 0.25 chord 0.554-0.651 (AR-017, T101_results.json C3 runs T101C3_*); default 1.0; verify on bench param dump, TP-19.
TECS_SPDWEIGHT,0.5
ARSPD_TYPE,1
ARSPD_BUS,0
ARSPD_TUBE_ORDR,2
ARSPD_USE,1
RUDD_DT_GAIN,35
YAW2SRV_DAMP,0.1
YAW2SRV_SLIP,0
INS_GYRO_RATE,0
# QP-3 follow-up 2: 60 Hz (was 40): the 2-pole gyro filter lag at 12-15 Hz was what turned the cage pitch mode unstable (fu_cage.py)
INS_GYRO_FILTER,60
# QP-4 / D-186: hover 1P is 100-119 Hz (prop_a.py 6,018-7,151 rpm for 1.38 kg to 8 m/s lean; the 71-76 Hz and the 70 Hz here were the 9545-era figures). Mode 1 = throttle reference (fallback, bidirectional DShot NOT confirmed);
#   MODE 3 only after M4 confirms rpm on the Kakute (then also SERVO_BLH_BDMASK 15). Base 105 Hz at hover throttle (6,272 rpm at the 1.50 kg gate) with REF 0.42 = Q_M_THST_HOVER, BW 40, harmonics 1st + 2nd; final values from the first IMU FFT. Cruise 1P is 122-127 Hz (7,300-7,600 rpm)
INS_HNTCH_ENABLE,1
INS_HNTCH_MODE,1
INS_HNTCH_REF,0.42
INS_HNTCH_FREQ,105
INS_HNTCH_BW,40
INS_HNTCH_HMNCS,3
INS_LOG_BAT_MASK,1
INS_LOG_BAT_OPT,5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 6 Battery and failsafes (K09-L lessons)
BATT_MONITOR,4
BATT_VOLT_MULT,11.05
BATT_AMP_PERVLT,64
# A: one Tattu 2300 mAh 4S 75C pack in flight (D-183b: the 2300, not the CNHL 3000; mission_gate_a.py: 24.5 Wh usable of 34.0 Wh). Two packs are bought, flown one at a time
BATT_CAPACITY,2800
# T-083: Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX 72 A = XT90 90 A / 1.25 (A-P16); four X2216 V3 on the APC 9x4.5MR draw 73 A at full duty on a fresh pack (prop_a.py EST), so it binds only there (duty 0.993).
# T-083: BATT_CAPACITY 2800 (O4b RDQ 2800 pack; was 2300 stale). BATT_LOW_MAH 790 = 2800 - 0.72 x 2800 (784, rounded up); BATT_CRT_MAH 420 = 345 x 2800 / 2300.
# remaining-capacity triggers (was, 2300 pack): usable = 0.90 worn-pack floor x 0.80 (20 % reserve) = 72 % of 2300 = 1656 mAh, so BATT_LOW fires at 2300 - 1656 = 644, set 650 mAh left (28 %).
#   That budget covers hover 180 s incl the 40 s go-around, two transitions, climb and 4.71 min of cruise at 1.396 kg (MISSION.md s4) (3.41 min needed). Critical at 15 % = 345 mAh
BATT_LOW_MAH,790
BATT_CRT_MAH,420
BATT_LOW_VOLT,14.4
BATT_CRT_VOLT,14.0
BATT_FS_VOLTSRC,1
# K09-L S8: in a hover mode a low battery must QLAND (6), not RTL, because RTL starts a forward transition at hover throttle
BATT_FS_LOW_ACT,6
BATT_FS_CRT_ACT,4
BATT_ARM_VOLT,16.0
SERIAL6_PROTOCOL,23
RSSI_TYPE,3
RC_OPTIONS,8480
THR_FAILSAFE,1
# K09-L S7: RC loss declared 1.0 s after the last frame, QLAND in Q modes within 1.2 s
RC_FS_TIMEOUT,1.0
FS_SHORT_ACTN,0
FS_LONG_ACTN,1
FS_LONG_TIMEOUT,5
FS_GCS_ENABL,0
Q_RTL_MODE,2
RTL_ALTITUDE,50
Q_RTL_ALT,50
Q_FW_LND_APR_RAD,60
RTL_RADIUS,60
# QP-3 follow-up 4: the cruise BATT_LOW action (BATT_FS_LOW_ACT 6, loiter to Q_RTL_ALT then QLAND) circles at this radius about the trigger point; 40 m (bank 36 deg at 17 m/s, stall 13.6 m/s) cut the
#   outward excursion from 70 to 49 m (SITL, 1.50 kg); the racetrack keeps R 51 m (flight card). QP-4 / BOARD s3: leg <= 150 m (any-direction bound L/2 + 51 + 94 = 220 m vs 240 m, MISSION.md s2), not 200 m
WP_LOITER_RAD,40
Q_TRANS_DECEL,2.0
FS_EKF_THRESH,0.8

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 7 Switches, fence, sensors
# K09-L R9 slot order on CH6: QSTABILIZE, FBWA, CRUISE, QHOVER, RTL, QLOITER
FLTMODE_CH,6
FLTMODE1,17
FLTMODE2,5
FLTMODE3,7
FLTMODE4,18
FLTMODE5,11
